  "notes": [
   "The breadboard in the image has rows a-e in its lower half and f-j in its upper half; by the catalogue naming, bank 't' = rows a-e (lower half in the image) and bank 'b' = rows f-j (upper half).",
   "The pushbutton straddles the centre gap at columns 10 and 12. Its legs in column 10 are treated as side 1 and its legs in column 12 as side 2. Pressing the button joins column 10 to column 12.",
   "The signal wire runs from D2 to column 10 (row c). The black wire runs from column 12 (row c) to the Arduino GND pin in the power header, which I mapped to GND.2.",
   "No external resistor is used. The internal pull-up on pin 2 (INPUT_PULLUP) supplies the pull-up. The onboard pin-13 LED is part of the Uno, so I added no external LED.",
   "The USB cable to the computer is implied for serial communication but is not shown in the circuit image, so I left it out."
  ]
 },
